        "original_id": "c7013240-5bbc-5a8e-ac08-15f16400e5d7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Brian Olsen, Mike Kyle, Frank Fertitta III, Lorenzo Fertitta\n- Companies: Zuffa, Station Casinos, Semaphore Entertainment Group\n- Organizations: WEC, UFC\n- Events: WEC 20\n- Titles: WEC Heavyweight Championship\n- Places: Las Vegas, Nevada\n\nFacts:\n- In January 2001, Zuffa was founded in Las Vegas, Nevada, by Station Casinos executives Frank Fertitta III and Lorenzo Fertitta.\n- In January 2001, Frank Fertitta III and Lorenzo Fertitta created Zuffa as the parent entity of the UFC after purchasing the UFC from Semaphore Entertainment Group.\n- At WEC 20, the main event was a heavyweight bout between Brian Olsen and Mike Kyle.\n- Brian Olsen was the last WEC Heavyweight Champion before the title was abolished when Zuffa purchased the WEC organization.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
